# XSH posix_madvise
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
# posix_madvise() returns an error number (not -1). Ranges are inside
# anonymous private mappings of whole pages, with {PAGESIZE} from sysconf().
# The advice must not change the contents. A hole inside the address space is
# not used for ENOMEM (the page says 'outside the range allowed'); a range
# that runs past the end of the address space is.

assertion  XSH.posix_madvise.001
anchor     functions/posix_madvise.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_madvise.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       posix_madvise() over a 4-page mapping returns 0 for each of
           POSIX_MADV_NORMAL, SEQUENTIAL, RANDOM, WILLNEED and DONTNEED.
test       t/001-advice-ok.c

assertion  XSH.posix_madvise.002
anchor     functions/posix_madvise.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       Contents of a private anonymous mapping (a pattern written before) are
           unchanged after each advice value, and can still be written and read back
           afterwards.
test       t/002-no-effect.c

assertion  XSH.posix_madvise.003
anchor     functions/posix_madvise.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       posix_madvise() with an advice value that is none of the five returns
           EINVAL (as the return value) over a valid range.
test       t/003-einval-advice.c

assertion  XSH.posix_madvise.004
anchor     functions/posix_madvise.html#ERRORS/ENOMEM
class      conditional
when       ADV
since      2001
says       posix_madvise() starting inside a mapping with a length that runs past the
           end of the address space returns ENOMEM.
test       t/004-enomem.c
